{
  "text": "[Warm, conversational voice, measured delivery] You have an idea worth explaining. [pause for 0.25 seconds] You want your audience to understand it well enough to act. [pause for 0.25 seconds] This repository turns explanations into videos, with narration and diagrams that move together.\n\n[pause for 1.25 seconds]\n\nRemotion turns React code, using web technologies such as HTML, CSS, and SVG, into video.\n\n[pause for 1.25 seconds]\n\nYou can start with an essay. [pause for 0.25 seconds] An AI coding agent uses the repository's skills to shape the script, generate the voiceover, and build a video around it. [pause for 0.25 seconds] The diagrams follow the spoken explanation.\n\n[pause for 1.25 seconds]\n\nOr start with a recording: a podcast, an interview, or a discussion. [pause for 0.25 seconds] The original voice and sequence stay intact. [pause for 0.25 seconds] The agent maps the ideas to timed visuals, so the explanation develops as you listen.\n\n[pause for 1.25 seconds]\n\nSkills give the agent instructions for these tasks. [pause for 0.25 seconds] Generate video essay guides the adaptation, with generate essay audio handling narration. [pause for 0.25 seconds] Animate recorded audio guides the workflow when the recording already exists.\n\n[pause for 1.25 seconds]\n\nThis video was made with the repository's custom-built Animation SDK. [pause for 0.25 seconds] An AI agent wrote the script, generated the voiceover with ElevenLabs, and used the SDK to animate the diagrams you're seeing. [pause for 0.25 seconds] The same toolkit is now explaining its own technical documentation.\n\n[pause for 1.25 seconds]\n\n[Softening, reflective] Start with something you want to explain, and ask your AI coding agent to make a video. [pause for 0.75 seconds]",
